<title>CHINA: Sino-U.S. power plant planned in China's Qingdao.</title>
<headline>Sino-U.S. power plant planned in China's Qingdao.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>China and the United States signed an agreement on Wednesday to build a $29.8 million gas turbine power plant in Qingdao city in China's eastern province of Shandong, the Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The U.S. partner would have an 80 percent stake with the remaining 20 percent taken up by the Chinese side, Xinhua said without identifying the partners.</p>
<p>The plant would have power generating capacity of 100 megawatts, it said.</p>
<p>Construction of the plant, covering an area of five hectares, was due to be completed in two years, Xinhua said without giving further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
